 "schema": "pcc.claim/v1",
 "scope": "research/p256_genus_dlp_20261115/minimal_transport",
 "statement": "For the fixed existing P-256 order and cubic eigenvalue, every nonzero integer coefficient pair satisfying the finite eigenline congruence has Eisenstein norm at least n. An explicitly assumed polarization coefficient 2Q is at least2n. A norm-n vector in the opposite-sign sector has both magnitudes below2^128. These integer endpoints are compiled/kernel-audited; the full Jacobian bridge, existence proof and native map qualification are separate obligations."
